##
# @SGIModelIoBoardPreset:
#
# Which base I/O board design a board record fits: the functions each
# preset's Bridge carries are a design fact of the board and are not
# carried here (`sgi-baseio`'s own preset table does).
#
# @ip29-io: Origin 200's integrated IP29 System Board I/O
#
# @ip29-io-crosstown: the same IP29 I/O with the GIGAchannel's
#     Crosstown extension board fitted in place of the XTalk
#     jumper board (SGI's name for it in the GIGAchannel upgrade
#     instructions, 108-0187-001 Figure 2-3), which adds its own
#     board record beside the IP29's
#
# @io6: the Origin 2000/Onyx2 plain BaseIO XIO card
#
# @ip30: onboard IP30 Bridge, dual ISP1040, IOC3 and RAD population
#
# @io6g: the Origin 2000/Onyx2 BaseIO-G XIO card, whose MediaIO
#     daughtercard adds a second IOC3 (keyboard, mouse, two serial
#     ports and a parallel port, no ethernet) alongside the plain
#     @io6 board's own
#
# @io8: the Origin 300 IO-8
#
# @fuel: Fuel IP34 system board I/O on XBridge head F
#
# @io9: the IO-9
#
# @pci-shoehorn: the Origin 2000 PCI-XTALK ADAPTER (PCI shoehorn), a
#     removable XIO card carrying one PCI card, fitted with an SGI Cad
#     Duo input card
#
# @pci-carrier: the Origin 2000 PCI Carrier Assembly, a removable XIO
#     card with three empty PCI slots
#
# @gigachannel: the Origin 200 GIGAchannel expansion cabinet's own
#     Bridge, with four empty PCI slots
#
# @menet: the Origin 2000/Onyx2 MENET XIO card, four IOC3s giving four
#     Fast Ethernet ports and six serial ports
#
# @kona: KONA, the Origin 2000/Onyx2 InfiniteReality graphics pipe,
#     an XIO card carrying no PCI function or IOC3 of its own; the
#     widget's identity is fixed by the device, so the record's @part,
#     @revision and @serial are not presented to the guest
#
# @mscsi: the MSCSI XIO card, four QLogic ISP1040 SCSI controllers
#
# @odyssey: a V12 widget wired straight to a node's XBridge
#     external port, as the Fuel's graphics board is at widget 13
#
# @vbrick: a V-brick enclosure, with its own XBridge and V12 board,
#     cabled to a node's XBridge external port; a neutral object marks
#     the L1 position.  Its processor route is a QEMU projection.  No
#     topology uses it
#
# @mgras: the SI/MXI (MGRAS) graphics board, an XIO card whose widget
#     answers XIO directly with no Bridge; the widget's own
#     identity is fixed by the device, so the record's @part,
#     @revision and @serial are not presented to the guest
#
# Since: 11.2
##
{ 'enum': 'SGIModelIoBoardPreset',
  'data': ['ip29-io', 'ip29-io-crosstown', 'ip30', 'io6', 'io6g', 'io8', 'fuel', 'io9',
           'pci-shoehorn', 'pci-carrier', 'gigachannel', 'menet', 'kona',
           'mscsi', 'mgras', 'odyssey', 'vbrick'] }

